ate semantic.cljc line numbers, added 4 direct mint sites in pipeline.cljc, yin/vm.cljc, storage.cljc), P3 (removed dead set element in equality-form?, documented canonical encoder exception narrowing in segment-matches?).\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:6541:- Confined JS IEEE-754 numbers to CLJS host boundary via js-number-class:\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:6542:  safe integers classify as :int64, non-integers as :double, and unsafe\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:6543:  integers return nil (diagnostic per value table).\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:6554:- Reconciled all findings from Adversarial Reviewer (P1 CLJS unsafe integers,\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:6736:    detects distinct equal-sequence equivocation, and enforces strictly\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:6737:    rising sequence numbers with cryptographic proofs.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:6840:  attributed to a \"documented JavaScript float64 carrier limitation\" —\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:6870:  Node evidence confirms the r2 P1 (float64 carrier rejection in\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:7340:  cljstyle clean; kondo 0 errors, warnings equal to the base.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:7351:  fail-open; declared-discharge threw on an unknown kind; profile\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:7358:- S5: glm authored (docs); sonnet APPROVE-WITH-FIXES (UCF 7.5.4 kind\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:7444:  1. Middleware: \"dao.stream should have ring-like middleware to add things like encryption, authentication/authorization capability tokens, or other custom transformation\". fable, gpt-6-sol and deepseek all READY TO SPECIFY the mechanism: a handle wrapper over the same protocol (declared data plus pure transforms, no ambient closures), position-preserving (cursors, anchors, gap, outcome kinds cross unchanged; a filter that drops elements is an interpreter, not middleware), two attachment points (per-stream on the table entry / reflection; per-channel for whole-message encryption), new dao.stream.middleware.md.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:8354:(measure first;