o\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:8841:Done: OWNER, verbatim: \"accept all recommendations\" (11 decisions). D6/D7: (1) structural equality on Closure/Continuation\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:8842:(kind, owner, payload); (2) cell/stream/cursor refs stay sealed plain data; (3) refuse non-symbol parameters now, move the\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:8843:store context off the lexical env later (slice C); (4) add data/number? and data/callable?. Safepoints: (5) a generic\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:8864:fixed P1/P2 and all P3s. Committed daf1c797, rebased cleanly onto 6b8502fd -> 7a8493e1 (py/numeric? keeps data/number?).\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9062:2722/187957/0, Node green, CLJD -1 (prelude-parity signed-zero-floats-on-every-host-test: py/zero-like loses the sign on\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9063:ClojureDart). Orchestrator tried building zeros as (- (* 1.0 0)) — no change; reverted (hypothesis \"integral float\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9081:the ClojureDart unary-minus fix ((- x) is 0 - x on CLJD; floats now negated with (* -1.0 x)). Gates: qwen3.8-max r1 (cmd),\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9097:  the big-integer design (Python C3) to the Architect; host-side debug inspector for opaque closures (recommended defer);\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9119:preservation), and 24cdf535 (unary float negation) were landed by a\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9158:  9 owner decisions) and C3 findings (reuse Jing's exact-integer carriers + CBOR tags 2/3 — no new wire format; fix\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9188:  tags 2/3 unchanged — no new payload kind; carrier recognition in encoder/heap/pin-refs/kind-of/data-number?\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9189:  tested on Node and Dart before any bignum reaches a cell; versioned :pure integer module over a per-host shim;\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9196:  C3-S1 integer-module + carrier-recognition engineer (worktree datomworld-py-c3int1, branch yang-python-c3-s1, brief\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9252:  migrate ucf.cljc to :yin.safepoint/kinds, new yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9270:  converged mob rulings as 8.5.3; C3 integers per the astra design and 14 converged mob rulings as 8.5.4; plus\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9308:  link-request acceptance (equal id+envelope maps to the same attempt;\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9309:  equal id different envelope refuses; bounded attempt records);\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9321:  evidence, never a new :yin.safepoint/kinds entry.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9349:## 2026-10-02 03:10:00 +07 — C3-S1 landed and pushed 54536317 (exact-integer module + carrier recognition)\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9356:  datomworld-py-c3int1, branch yang-python-c3-s1): the versioned :pure integer module (yin.vm.integer +\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9357:  integer/host shim, 487+240 lines) per converged rulings 1/2/5/11 — exact kernels written once over the per-host\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9361:  (:bit-limit/:digit-limit as ex-info data), and scalar carrier recognition in engine/scalar?, values/kind-of,\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9362:  data/number? (encoder, heap trace, pin-refs) + a 6-line UCF scalar-arm clarification (ruling 4: no marker, no\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9390:  identity and index only, over remote ring streams, with B0-equality\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9531:  JavaScript number)\" — the base prelude's C1 integer-bound literals at prelude.cljc:560,561,572,748 are beyond\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9532:  JS safe-integer hashing. Pre-existing latent defect (C1 line) surfaced because slice 1's safepoint tests are\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9556:  54536317 C3-S1 exact-integer module + carrier recognition (my lanes JVM 2857/226101/0, Node 2674/91509/0, CLJD\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9571:  Node blocker: dao.jing.cbor refuses the base prelude's C1 integer-bound literals (prelude.cljc:560,561,572,748)\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9572:  as unsafe integral JS numbers, blocking full-prelude projection on Node. Fix round 2 brief is\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9680:  (verified: empty diff on cbor.cljc);