{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yang/safepoint_test.cljc | sed -n '1,135p'; nl -ba docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md | sed -n '512,530p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc | sed -n '630,646p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yang.safepoint-test\n     2\t  \"The language-neutral safepoint stage over a small hand-built tree, on\n     3\t   every host: insertion at marked lambdas, tail marks recomputed, the\n     4\t   identity on an empty profile, refusals, and golden addresses that every\n     5\t   host must reproduce (insertion determinism across CLJ, CLJS and CLJD).\"\n     6\t  (:require\n     7\t    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n     8\t    [dao.jing :as jing]\n     9\t    [yang.safepoint :as safepoint]\n    10\t    [yang.tails :as tails]\n    11\t    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    12\t    [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]))\n    13\t\n    14\t\n    15\t(defn- v\n    16\t  [s]\n    17\t  {:type :variable, :name s})\n    18\t\n    19\t\n    20\t(defn- app\n    21\t  [op & args]\n    22\t  {:type :application, :operator op, :operands (vec args)})\n    23\t\n    24\t\n    25\t(defn- lam\n    26\t  [params body]\n    27\t  {:type :lambda, :params params, :body body})\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\t(defn- site\n    31\t  [kind node]\n    32\t  (vary-meta node assoc :yang/site kind))\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\t(def ^:private ast\n    36\t  \"`((fn [w] (w w)) (fn [w] (f w)))`, both lambdas marked: the first a\n    37\t   `:call` site, the second a `:loop` site; tails marked as a frontend\n    38\t   would.\"\n    39\t  (tails/mark-tails\n    40\t    (app (site :call (lam '[w] (app (v 'w) (v 'w))))\n    41\t         (site :loop (lam '[w] (app (v 'f) (v 'w)))))))\n    42\t\n    43\t\n    44\t(def ^:private profile {:loop 'h/loop, :call 'h/call})\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\t(defn- projected\n    48\t  []\n    49\t  (encoder/project (encoder/source-envelope :m [:t 0] [ast])))\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\t(defn- derived\n    53\t  [p]\n    54\t  (safepoint/derive-envelope (projected) p :m'))\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\t(defn- tree\n    58\t  [e]\n    59\t  (nth (:yin/batch e) (:yin/root e)))\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\t(deftest sites-from-the-side-table-test\n    63\t  (let [e (projected)]\n    64\t    (is (= {[2] :call, [[3 0]] :loop}\n    65\t           (safepoint/sites (:yin/frontend-metadata e)\n    66\t                            (vm/source-origin :m [:t 0] 0)\n    67\t                            (:root (tree e)))))))\n    68\t\n    69\t\n    70\t(deftest insertion-test\n    71\t  (let [out (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast (tree (:envelope (derived profile))))\n    72\t        hooked (fn [hook body]\n    73\t                 {:type :application,\n    74\t                  :operator {:type :lambda, :params ['yang.safepoint/_], :body body},\n    75\t                  :operands [{:type :application,\n    76\t                              :operator {:type :variable, :name hook},\n    77\t                              :operands [],\n    78\t                              :tail? false}],\n    79\t                  :tail? true})]\n    80\t    (testing \"each marked lambda's body runs after its hook; the hook\n    81\t              application is an operand, never a tail call, and the old body\n    82\t              is a tail call of the sequencing lambda\"\n    83\t      (is (= {:type :application,\n    84\t              :operator {:type :lambda, :params '[w],\n    85\t                         :body (hooked 'h/call\n    86\t                                       {:type :application, :operator {:type :variable, :name 'w},\n    87\t                                        :operands [{:type :variable, :name 'w}], :tail? true})},\n    88\t              :operands [{:type :lambda, :params '[w],\n    89\t                          :body (hooked 'h/loop\n    90\t                                        {:type :application,\n    91\t                                         :operator {:type :variable, :name 'f},\n    92\t                                         :operands [{:type :variable, :name 'w}],\n    93\t                                         :tail? true})}],\n    94\t              :tail? false}\n    95\t             out)))))\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\t(deftest profile-selects-kinds-test\n    99\t  (let [{:keys [envelope record]} (derived {:loop 'h/loop})\n   100\t        out (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast (tree envelope))]\n   101\t    (testing \"a kind the profile omits is not inserted\"\n   102\t      (is (= (tails/strip-tails (:operator ast))\n   103\t             (tails/strip-tails (:operator out)))))\n   104\t    (is (= {:yang.safepoint/hooks {:loop 'h/loop},\n   105\t            :yang.safepoint/sites (jing/segment-key [[[[3 0]] :loop]])}\n   106\t           (:yin.ledger/profile record)))))\n   107\t\n   108\t\n   109\t(deftest empty-profile-is-the-identity-test\n   110\t  (let [{:keys [envelope record]} (derived {})]\n   111\t    (is (= (tree (projected)) (tree envelope)))\n   112\t    (is (= (:yin.ledger/input record) (:yin.ledger/output record)))))\n   113\t\n   114\t\n   115\t(deftest remark-reproduces-a-frontends-marks-test\n   116\t  (is (= ast (tails/remark-tails ast))))\n   117\t\n   118\t\n   119\t(deftest refusals-test\n   120\t  (let [t (tree (projected))]\n   121\t    (testing \"a site that names a node that is not a lambda\"\n   122\t      (is (= :site-not-lambda\n   123\t             (try (safepoint/insert t {[] :loop} profile) nil\n   124\t                  (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n   125\t                    (:rule (ex-data e)))))))\n   126\t    (testing \"a site that names no node\"\n   127\t      (is (= :site-missing\n   128\t             (try (safepoint/insert t {[9] :loop} profile) nil\n   129\t                  (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n   130\t                    (:rule (ex-data e)))))))))\n   131\t\n   132\t\n   133\t(deftest every-host-derives-the-same-addresses-test\n   134\t  (let [{:keys [envelope record-address]} (derived profile)]\n   135\t    (is (nil? (vm/validate-rows (tree envelope))))\n   512\t## Addressing and clean break\n   513\t\n   514\tHash canonical payload bytes directly with the selected registry algorithm,\n   515\tper [`dao.jing.hash-registry.md`](dao.jing.hash-registry.md): BLAKE3 by\n   516\tdefault, SHA-256 by explicit selection. Preserve the address shape\n   517\t`:segment/<algorithm-id>-<64 lowercase hex>`, with canonical forms\n   518\t`:segment/blake3-<64 lowercase hex>` and `:segment/sha256-<64 lowercase\n   519\thex>`. Keep the existing string-based `sha256` helper for its other callers\n   520\tand add separate byte-hashing functions for each registered algorithm.\n   521\t\n   522\tEvery newly encoded value receives its CBOR-derived address. No legacy\n   523\treader, old-address alias, or graph migration is included. Reject old\n   524\tcomplete EDN file records without rewriting them. Existing stores and\n   525\tpublished references must be rebuilt together, including address-bearing\n   526\tindexes, ASTs, and continuations. **This states the rebuild's precondition\n   527\texplicitly: with no legacy reader, the only reconstruction path is\n   528\treplaying original values from their intake streams, not reading them back\n   529\tout of a rejected old store.** A value whose intake stream has since\n   530\tevicted it (a `:dao.stream/gap`) and whose old store is rejected under this\n   630\t\n   631\t\n   632\t(defn- scalar?\n   633\t  \"True for a value that holds nothing: UCF 7.5.1's scalar arm, also the\n   634\t   leaf test of the heap trace and of pinning. An exact-integer carrier\n   635\t   is a scalar on every host, including a JS or Dart big integer, which\n   636\t   answers false to `number?` (C3 ruling 4).\"\n   637\t  [x]\n   638\t  (or (nil? x) (boolean? x) (number? x) (integer-host/big-carrier? x)\n   639\t      (string? x) (keyword? x) (symbol? x)))\n   640\t\n   641\t\n   642\t(defn- encode-primitive\n   643\t  \"A host function as UCF 7.5.2's primitive marker: its one name in\n   644\t   `vm`'s primitives, with that name's profile address.\"\n   645\t  [vm f]\n   646\t  (let [n (vm/name-of (:primitives vm)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
